{
"id":9703152550127,
"title":"Chelbesa Danche",
"handle":"chelbesa-danche",
"body_html":"<p>Chelbesa Danche is practically a household name in specialty coffee, and this lot is about as clean &amp; fruity as it gets. The flavors are layered orange and tart cherry, with even a hint of pineapple, grape, and raspberry. The aromas are rose and powdered sugary blueberries. This is classic, washed Ethiopian coffee.</p>\n<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-dfa67e7 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"dfa67e7\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\"><span>This coffee is named for the Danche washing station where it's produced. Approximately 800 farmers deliver their coffee cherries to this washing station, each farming 2-3 hectares of land at 2200 meters. </span></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-d6bd752 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"d6bd752\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n<span>Only ripe cherries were picke, then they were floated to remove defects. Next the coffee was pulped, dry-fermented for 96 hours, and then fully washed. The coffee then dried for 12-14 days on raised beds.</span><span></span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n<span></span><br>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>Process: Washed</p>\n<p>Variety: Kurume &amp; Wolisho</p>\n<p>Region: Gedeb, Ethiopia</p>\n<p><strong><em>Make sure to check that the roast date you've selected is what you're looking for </em></strong><em>— if there is an</em><strong><em> </em></strong><em>\"upcoming roast\" for this coffee, the upcoming roast date is listed under the tasting notes at the top of this product page.</em></p>\n<p><em><a href=\"https://getprodigal.com/pages/shipping-information\"><strong>Please read our shipping info page!</strong></a></em></p>",
